# Being listed HERE is a promise the suite keeps by running the block: if one of
# these stops exiting 0, `running_every_block_agrees_with_the_bucket_it_is_in`
# fails and the block has to move to the KNOWN-FAIL file, with the first line of
# stderr it now prints. That is the whole point of listing the working blocks
# at all: without this file a block that stopped working would silently join the
# fragments, and a documentation promise would rot without a word.
#
# "Runs" means BOTH runners now. `rb run` has to exit 0 AND `rb compile` has to
